# UI design (this portfolio)

## Design tokens — use existing CSS variables

From `public/css/moh-layout.css` — do not invent a new palette:

- `--navy`, `--blue`, `--sky-moh`, `--green-moh`, `--gold`
- `--ink`, `--body-moh`, `--pale`, `--line-moh`, `--header-blue`

Extend tokens in that file when needed; reuse classes/patterns already there.

## Layout

- Hero: brand + one headline + one short sentence + CTA; full-bleed; no cards/badges overlays on hero
- Cards only when they wrap a real interaction; otherwise open layout
- One section = one job + one headline + one short supporting line
- Mobile-first; readable on phone
- Motion: 2–3 intentional transitions (hover/reveal), not animation noise

## Avoid (generic AI look)

- Purple/indigo gradients, cream + terracotta cliché, dark neon glow
- Pill clusters, stat strips, floating promo badges on hero
- New competing themes that ignore MOH colors

## Reuse

Prefer shared pieces under `src/Web/Shared/` and existing `moh-layout.css` over duplicating styles.
